# Build output and generated dependencies, unanchored on purpose: these are what
# they are wherever they sit, and firmware/ is not the only place they appear —
# the spikes were their own ESP-IDF projects and generated the whole set beside
# themselves, which the anchored rules never reached. One configuration leaves
# ~15 MB of liblvgl__lvgl.a alone, sdkconfig is rewritten on every reconfigure,
# and output that is merely untracked rather than ignored is what agent tooling
# snapshots into the object store, where no commit hook or CI job will see it.
#
# The cost of dropping the anchors is that a source directory named build/ or
# build-*/ would now disappear from git add without a word. Nothing in the tree
# is named that today, and a build directory anywhere is far likelier to be
# output than source; a source directory that wants one of these names can be
# unignored as a directory with an explicit ! rule. As a directory is the whole
# of it — git does not descend into an excluded one, so !docs/build/keep.md is
# silently still ignored where !docs/build/ re-includes what is under it.
build/
build-*/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
managed_components/
node_modules/

# firmware/dependencies.lock is NOT ignored. It records the exact component
# versions a build resolved, and joltwallet/littlefs decides the on-disk
# filesystem format — an unpinned upgrade is a silently reformatted partition
# on the first boot after an OTA.

# Generated LVGL fonts. The sources of truth are tools/fonts/icons.txt and
# tools/fonts/generate.sh; the generated sources would otherwise add ~1.1 MB
# of unreviewable hex to every glyph-list change, permanently.
# Run tools/fonts/generate.sh before building the firmware.
firmware/components/slate_theme/assets/slate_font_*.c
firmware/components/slate_theme/assets/slate_icons.h

# Generator scratch — upstream TTFs are fetched into tools/fonts/.work/, not
# vendored. Unanchored with the rest above; .github/workflows/ci.yml caches that
# directory by path, which actions/cache resolves without consulting .gitignore.
.work/

# The editor's build output. The bundle is a ~200 KB single-file document
# generated from editor/src; the firmware build compresses whatever is in dist/
# into the image (DESIGN.md §10), so it is generated before a build the way the
# fonts above are. Its node_modules/ is covered by the rule at the top.
# Run tools/editor/build.sh before building the firmware.
#
# dist/ keeps its anchor where build/ lost one: a directory named dist is as
# often vendored as generated, and these two are generated by named scripts, so
# the rule says which ones rather than claiming every dist in the tree.
editor/dist/

# The directory tools/flasher/build.sh assembles for deployment, carrying the
# vendored ESP Web Tools bundle it copies out of node_modules/ — which is itself
# covered by the rule at the top. dist/ contains a copy of the firmware images
# as well, so it is build output twice over: flasher/index.html and
# flasher/package-lock.json are the sources of truth, and
# .github/workflows/release.yml regenerates the rest on every tag.
flasher/dist/

.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from the helpers in tools/
__pycache__/

# Scratch notes agents pass between themselves while working the same
# repository — plans, todo lists, half-finished findings. They belong to a
# workspace rather than to a change, so `git add -A` must not sweep them into
# the repository's history. Unanchored on purpose: scratch is scratch wherever
# it sits, and nothing tracked is named .context.
.context/
